            <div xml:id="d812">

                <pb facs="0939" n="843" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg843"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">816.51/64: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Salvador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Arnold</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San Salvador</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-05-18T09:00:00-06:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 18, 1921—9
                                a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 8:10 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>24. President Meléndez informs me that he is negotiating a loan of $10,000,000
                    through Bloom Brothers, an American firm New York, to be guaranteed by a
                    percentage of the customhouse receipts. The lenders will appoint a controller of
                    the customhouses of the Republic.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Arnold</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
